 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Extension closure and zero objects of t-structure bounds",
 "statement": "Let $t$ be a t-structure on a triangulated category $\\mathcal T$ [def-weil-t-structure]. For every integer $n$, every zero object belongs to both $\\mathcal T^{\\le n}$ and $\\mathcal T^{\\ge n}$. If $X\\to Y\\to Z\\to X[1]$ is distinguished and $X,Z\\in\\mathcal T^{\\le n}$, then $Y\\in\\mathcal T^{\\le n}$; if $X,Z\\in\\mathcal T^{\\ge n}$, then $Y\\in\\mathcal T^{\\ge n}$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/bbd-faisceaux-pervers_Asterisque-100-1982.pdf",
  "place": "1.3.4, orthogonality and extension closure, p. 30"
 },
